%H A400547 Michael Laszlo and Sumitra Mukherjee, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s11786-023-00558-7">Counting Star-Battle Configurations</a>, Mathematics in Computer Science 17 (2023), Art. 8.
%H A400547 Igor Minevich, Gabe Cunningham, K. Aditya Karan, and Joshua V. Gyllinsky, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.02251">Parks: A Doubly Infinite Family of NP-Complete Puzzles and Generalizations of A002464</a>, arXiv:2411.02251 [cs.CC], 2024. See Sections V and VIII.
%H A400547 Thomas Snyder, <a href="https://www.gmpuzzles.com/blog/star-battle-rules-and-info/">Star Battle Rules and Info</a>, The Art of Puzzles, Jan 15 2013.
%H A400547 Thomas Snyder, <a href="https://www.gmpuzzles.com/blog/2024/09/bonus-star-battle-by-thomas-snyder/">Bonus: Star Battle (also known as Queens) by Thomas Snyder</a>, The Art of Puzzles, Sep 08 2024.
%F A400547 a(n) >= n*A002464(n) for n >= 1.
%e A400547 a(4) = 11760. One of these partitions, with the star cells in lower case:
%e A400547   A a A A
%e A400547   B A C c
%e A400547   b D D D
%e A400547   B D d D
%e A400547 The stars are at (row, column) = (1,2), (2,4), (3,1), (4,3). The only other placement allowed by the row, column and adjacency rules, (1,3), (2,1), (3,4), (4,2), has two stars in region D.
%e A400547 For n = 4 there are only two permutations with |p(i+1) - p(i)| >= 2, namely 2413 and 3142, so every partition has 0, 1 or 2 solutions. Of the A395493(4) = 62741 partitions, 49668 have no solution, 11760 have exactly one and 1313 have two.
